    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d176">

                <pb facs="0237" n="121" xml:id="pg121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/812.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to Great
                            Britain to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-21T17:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 21, 1912—5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your March 19, 8 p.m., which I read to Langley, Assistant Under Secretary of
                    State for Foreign Affairs. He replied that Belgian Minister in London had
                    already informally approached Foreign Office in the matter, and had been
                    answered in almost precisely the same language used in your proposed reply to
                    the Belgian Minister at Washington.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reid.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
